cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite the preferred citation
  (the workshop poster). The software record below is prism-bench 0.3.0.
type: software
title: >-
  PRISM: Pathology Reliability In Scarce-label Medicine.
  A Tile-level Benchmark of Pathology Foundation Models
authors:
  - family-names: Koyun
    given-names: Alicem
    affiliation: Westcliff University
version: 0.3.0
# Camera-ready date in CHANGELOG.md. PyPI prism-bench 0.3.0 was uploaded 2026-10-23.
date-released: "2026-10-04"
license: MIT
repository-code: https://github.com/alicemkyn/prism-benchmark
url: https://github.com/alicemkyn/prism-benchmark
abstract: >-
  PRISM measures the reliability of pathology foundation models at tile
  level under label scarcity and distribution shift, under one fixed
  frozen-embedding linear-probe protocol.
keywords:
  - pathology
  - foundation models
  - benchmark
  - calibration
  - label efficiency
  - distribution shift
  - temperature scaling
identifiers:
  - type: url
    value: https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.36517
    description: arXiv abstract of the workshop poster
  - type: other
    value: "arXiv:2610.36517"
    description: arXiv identifier
  - type: url
    value: https://pypi.org/project/prism-bench/
    description: PyPI package prism-bench (MIT, version 0.3.0)
  - type: url
    value: https://huggingface.co/datasets/alicemkyn/PRISM-embeddings
    description: >-
      Gated precomputed embeddings. Download requires accepting the
      dataset click-through agreement.
